Exit code: 0
---
Stdout:
ST901  Custom check failed                                                MEDIUM
checks user-defined

The API broke a rule that a custom check, registered with `@schemathesis.check`,
enforces.

Why it matters
  The check guards a rule the schema cannot express, such as an audit header on
  every write. When the API breaks it, whatever depends on that rule, such as an
  audit log, receives wrong or missing data.

Example
  @schemathesis.check
  def check_audit_trail(ctx, response, case):
      if case.method == "POST" and "x-audit-id" not in response.headers:
          raise AssertionError("Data modification missing audit trail")

    - ST901 Custom check failed: `check_audit_trail`

        Data modification missing audit trail

How Schemathesis found it
  Schemathesis runs every enabled check against each response. A check that
  raises `AssertionError` produces a failure titled "Custom check failed". The
  title carries the check's name in backticks: the function name, or the class
  name for a class-based check. The message below the title is the assertion
  message, empty when the assertion has none. Response header names reach the
  check in lowercase.

  A class-based check that fails in `after_run` shows under "Run checks", with
  no case ID. An unexpected exception there reads "Check `<name>` raised an
  unexpected error". A check that raises its own `Failure` subclass shows the
  title that subclass sets.

  To find the logic, search for `def <name>` or `class <name>` under
  `@schemathesis.check`. The CLI loads checks from the module or file named in
  `SCHEMATHESIS_HOOKS` or in the `hooks` key of schemathesis.toml. pytest loads
  them from `conftest.py`.

How to fix
  Decide whether the rule holds for the request in the failure.

  - It holds: the API is wrong. Fix the API for that request.
  - It does not: the check is wrong. Narrow it, for example skip operations or
    methods it does not cover. Until then, `[checks.<name>]` with `enabled =
    false` in schemathesis.toml turns it off.
  - The check raised an unexpected error: fix the bug in the check.

Verify the fix
  For a function check, run `st replay <case id>` with the same
  `SCHEMATHESIS_HOOKS` or `hooks` setting as the run. Without it, replay reports
  "check not available to re-run". Replay cannot rerun class-based checks or
  `after_run` failures, which have no case ID. For those, rerun `st run` and
  confirm the failure is gone.

Turn it off
  `--exclude-checks <name>`, where `<name>` is the custom check named in the failure,
  or in schemathesis.toml:
    [checks.<name>]
    enabled = false

Docs  https://schemathesis.readthedocs.io/en/stable/reference/failures/#st901
